  "note": "Election of 21 members for seven wards (three each) on 17 May 1961. Carnmoney, Jordanstown and Whitewell were uncontested; there were contests in Cavehill, Glengormley, Whiteabbey and Whitehouse. The fourth candidate, Joseph Clarence Taggart (U.), was not elected; his vote is lost in a damaged column of the Belfast News-Letter and is therefore omitted. Electorate 2,633; poll 37 per cent."
